---
import { withBase } from '../../lib/base'
import Icon from './Icon.astro'

const install = 'npx skills add AhmeddBasemm/docspp --skill docspp'
const points = [
  {
    icon: 'lucide:braces',
    title: 'A published JSON Schema',
    text: 'docspp schema writes it next to your diagrams. Editors autocomplete every key, and agents stop guessing them.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'lucide:map-pin',
    title: 'Errors that say where',
    text: 'File, line and column, with a hint that spells the right key. Add --json and a script can read them.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'lucide:shield-check',
    title: 'A broken diagram never ships',
    text: 'The build fails on diagram errors, so a typo is caught on the pull request and not on the live site.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'lucide:link',
    title: 'References that notice drift',
    text: 'List the source files a box is based on. docspp check warns when one of them moves.',
  },
]
---

<section class="lp-section lp-band" id="agents">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-head">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">For people and agents</p>
      <h2>Plain YAML that an agent can write and a machine can check.</h2>
      <p class="lp-lede">
        The format is small, the schema is published and the validator is strict. Ask Claude Code, Cursor or
        Copilot to draw your architecture, and the loop below keeps the result honest.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-agents-grid">
      <div class="lp-term" role="img" aria-label="A terminal session: an agent writes a diagram, docspp check reports two problems, the agent fixes them and the check passes.">
        <div class="lp-term-bar">claude code <span>diagrams/checkout</span></div>
<pre aria-hidden="true"><span class="you">you</span>    Add a diagram of how checkout works. The code is in services/.
       Include a scenario for a declined card.

<span class="ai">claude</span> Reading services/orders, services/catalog and the gateway config.
       Wrote diagrams/checkout/diagram.yaml  <span class="dim">(12 nodes, 4 scenarios)</span>

<span class="dim">$</span> <span class="cmd">pnpm docspp check</span>
diagrams/checkout/diagram.yaml:8:29  <span class="warn">warning</span>  Unknown icon "strpe"
    <span class="dim">Run `docspp icons search &lt;name&gt;` to find one.</span>
diagrams/checkout/diagram.yaml:13:5  <span class="err">error</span>  Edge to "paymnts" is not a node
1 diagram compiled in .: <span class="err">1 error</span>, <span class="warn">1 warning</span>

<span class="ai">claude</span> Two typos. Fixing both and checking again.

<span class="dim">$</span> <span class="cmd">pnpm docspp check</span>
1 diagram compiled in .: <span class="ok">0 errors, 0 warnings</span></pre>
      </div>

      <div>
        <ul class="lp-points">
          {
            points.map((p) => (
              <li>
                <Icon name={p.icon} />
                <div>
                  <strong>{p.title}</strong>
                  <p>{p.text}</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <div class="lp-agents-cta">
          <div class="lp-install">
            <span class="lp-prompt">$</span>
            <code>{install}</code>
            <button class="lp-copy" type="button" data-copy={install} aria-label="Copy command">
              <Icon name="lucide:copy" />
            </button>
          </div>
          <a class="lp-btn lp-btn-ghost" href={withBase('ai/skill/')}>About the skill</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
